            <ArticleTitle>Interaction between lipid availability,endurance exercise and insulin sensitivity.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>62-70</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1159/000357336</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>This chapter summarizes current knowledge regarding the interaction between lipid availability, endurance exercise, and insulin sensitivity. We discuss the role of lipid availability as a key mediator of insulin resistance in obesity, the proposed cellular mechanisms underlying this relationship, recent studies demonstrating that acute exercise protects against lipid-induced insulin resistance, how fatty acid partitioning may contribute to this protective effect of endurance exercise and finally remaining questions and future directions in the field.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
